NAME
       ldconfig - configure dynamic linker run-time bindings

SYNOPSIS
       ldconfig [-nNXvp] [DIR]...

DESCRIPTION
       Scan the directories given on the command line, the directories listed
       in /etc/ld.so.conf (including "include PATTERN" lines, for example
       include /etc/ld.so.conf.d/*.conf), then /lib and /usr/lib. For every
       ELF shared object found, read its DT_SONAME, create or update the
       symbolic link SONAME -> real file in the same directory (for example
       libfoo.so.1 -> libfoo.so.1.2.3) and write the cache /etc/ld.so.cache.
       The cache is written to a temporary file and renamed, so the loader
       never sees a partial file. If several files share one SONAME the one
       with the longest, then greatest, name wins. Writing needs root.

OPTIONS
       -n  process only the directories given on the command line; implies -N
       -N  do not rebuild the cache
       -X  do not update the symbolic links
       -v  verbose: show directories scanned and links created
       -p  print the contents of the cache (works for any user)

CONFIG FILE
       /etc/ld.so.conf has one directory per line; text after # is a comment.

CACHE FORMAT
       /etc/ld.so.cache is a text file. The first line is exactly

           PCLDCACHE1

       and every following line is

           SONAME<TAB>/absolute/path/to/library

       The dynamic loader reads it only when a library was not found through
       DT_RPATH, LD_LIBRARY_PATH or DT_RUNPATH. A missing, corrupt or stale
       file is ignored. The first entry for a SONAME wins.

ENVIRONMENT
       The loader honours LD_LIBRARY_PATH, LD_TRACE_LOADED_OBJECTS and
       LD_DEBUG=libs; see ldd(1).

FILES
       /etc/ld.so.conf, /etc/ld.so.conf.d/*.conf, /etc/ld.so.cache

SEE ALSO
       ldd(1)
